     "hint": "The lot holds spots and open tickets. A spot holds a size and who is in it. A ticket holds what exit needs for the fee and can say its own hours.",
     "solution": "class ParkingLot\n- spots: Spot[]  (lowest level first)  # enter scans in order for the first free fit\n- tickets: Map<ticket_id, Ticket>  # exit only gets an id; a map finds it in one step\n- next_id: int  # every ticket needs a unique id; a counter hands out the next\n+ enter(plate, size, now) -> Ticket | error  # req 1\n+ exit(ticket_id, now) -> fee in cents | error  # req 2 and 3: free the spot, price the stay\n+ free_count(size) -> int  # req 4: the sign at the gate\n\nclass Spot\n- spot_id: string  # printed on the ticket so the driver finds the car\n- size: Size  (SMALL, MEDIUM, LARGE -> enum)  # decides what fits\n- plate: string | None  # None means free; no separate flag\n+ fits(size) -> boolean  # the size rule lives in one place\n+ park(plate) -> void  # the spot changes its own state\n+ leave() -> void  # exit calls it to free the spot\n\nclass Ticket\n- ticket_id: int  # the key in the lot's map\n- plate: string  # catches the same car entering twice\n- size: Size  # the fee rate, without a second lookup\n- spot: Spot  # exit frees this spot directly\n- entered_at: datetime  # hours parked = now - entered_at\n+ hours_parked(now) -> int  # started hours, at least 1; the fee is this times the rate",
     "why": "Exit looks a ticket up by id, so a map keeps it to one step. The ticket stores the vehicle size so the fee needs no second lookup.",
