     "solution": "1. User adds an expense: a payer, an amount in cents, a group and a split.\n   - The system computes each person's share by the split type and records what each owes the payer\n   - Shares that don't total the amount, an unknown group or a non-member is an error\n2. User asks who owes whom.\n   - The system returns the net amount between two users, or one user's net against everyone\n3. User settles up by paying someone they owe.\n   - The system records it as a debt in the other direction\n   - Paying more than owed leaves the other person owing\n4. Out of scope: currencies (they will ask), simplifying debts (they will ask), login and notifications, persistence.",
