      {
       "q": "Why integer cents?",
       "a": "Floats cannot hold 0.10 exactly, so thirds and percents drift. Cents are ints, and the leftover rule makes every split total the amount to the cent."
      },
      {
       "q": "Why does the leftover go to the first people?",
       "a": "Any fixed rule works if it is stated and deterministic. First in the order given means the same input always gives the same shares."
      },
      {
       "q": "Is there a stdlib shortcut for the leftover?",
       "a": "Yes: the largest remainder method, or Decimal quantize. Writing the divmod loop shows the rule, and it is four lines."
      },
      {
       "q": "Why net per pair instead of per user?",
       "a": "Per pair answers 'who owes me' directly. Net per user loses who, which is why simplify_debts is a separate read."
      }
