     "solution": "1. Primary capabilities\n- Limit by what?\n- What is the limit?\n- What does the caller learn?\n\n2. Error handling\n- What happens when a client is over its limit?\n- A bad limit, such as zero or negative?\n- A request with no client id?\n\n3. Scope boundaries\n- Which algorithm?\n- How does time work? A real clock?\n- One server or many? Different limits per plan?",
     "why": "Every question changes a class or a method. A burst plus a rate gives Rule's two numbers. The wait in the answer is why allow returns a pair. Time passed in is why no class reads a clock, and the algorithm question tells me to put it behind one call, try_consume.",
