     "t": "write",
     "id": "ratelimiter-reqs-w",
     "q": "Write the requirements, numbered, then out of scope.",
     "starter": "1. \n2. \n3. \n",
     "hint": "A service asks, a bucket per client refilling with time, a rule with two numbers.",
     "solution": "1. A service asks whether a request from a client may go ahead.\n   - The limiter finds that client's bucket and takes a token if there is one\n   - Denies, with a retry-after, when the bucket is empty; an error for an empty client id\n2. Each client has its own bucket, full the first time it is seen.\n   - A bucket refills steadily with elapsed time, up to its capacity\n   - Time is passed in with each call; a time that has not moved, or goes backwards, adds nothing\n3. A rule sets the capacity (the burst) and the refill rate.\n   - A zero or negative rule is rejected when the Rule is built\n4. Out of scope: the HTTP layer and the 429 response, many servers, persistence, different limits per plan (an extension), a real clock.",
